title: Slingshots and breakable blocks
intro: A slingshot to pull back and let go, and towers of wood, glass and stone that crack and break on hard knocks, with no code.
project: Empty | Knock It Down

chapter: A slingshot and a tower | Entity > Genres > Physics Games
create: Slingshot
expectcount: Shot = 3
expectcount: Ground = 1
expectvalue: Main Camera.Follow.Target = Slingshot
explain: component:Slingshot | Slingshot | A slingshot, with three shots waiting behind it: the bodies inside it, launched in turn. Then it can make copies of a prefab, as many as its Shots says.
explain: field:Slingshot.Power | Power | Pull it all the way back and the shot leaves this fast; less, the less it's pulled.
explain: field:Slingshot.CameraFollows | The camera | The camera follows each shot as it flies, and comes back for the next.
deselect
create: Tower
expectcount: Plank = 1
expectcount: Target = 1
expectcount: Score = 1
say: The tower is two storeys of wood, a pane of glass and a stone slab, with a green target inside, all asleep until something hits them, and a score along the top.
select: Plank
explain: component:Breakable | Breakable | Each piece is breakable. A hit is as hard as the push it takes to stop it: mass times speed. Hits softer than Min Hit do nothing; harder ones add up, cracking it, and at its Strength it breaks.
explain: field:Breakable.Split | Pieces | It splits into pieces that tumble away and fade, with a puff of dust, its sound, and its Break Message carrying its points to the score.
deselect
create: Sprite
rename: Crate
set: Transform.Position = 3, 0.5, 0
set: Sprite.Tint = #B07F4A
menu: Entity > Add Breakable
expectcomponents: Crate = Transform, Sprite, BoxCollider, Body, Breakable
expectvalue: Crate.Body.Rotates = true
say: Add Breakable makes anything break on hard knocks: it gets a body that rotates, and a collider the size of its sprite.
set: Breakable.Strength = 4
deselect

chapter: Knock it down | Pull the pouch back and let go
play
wait: 1
expectvalue: Slingshot.Slingshot.Loaded = true
expectvalue: Slingshot.Slingshot.ShotsLeft = 3
gamedrag: Slingshot + 0, 1.6 > Slingshot + -1.8, 0.7
wait: 0.2
expectvalue: Slingshot.Slingshot.Loaded = false
expectvalue: Slingshot.Slingshot.ShotsLeft = 2
explain: game | Away it goes | Pulled back and let go, the shot flies off the other way, as fast as it was pulled, and the camera goes with it.
wait: 3
expectvalue: Score.Counter.Value = 10000 ~ 9999
say: Whatever it hits hard enough cracks and breaks into pieces, and what falls can break the next thing down.
wait: 6
expectvalue: Slingshot.Slingshot.Loaded = true
say: Once the shot has come to rest the next is loaded, and the camera comes back.
hold: Left+Down 0.6
explain: game | With the keys | With the keys or a gamepad the arrows pull the pouch about, and a dotted line shows where the shot will go. Space lets go.
tap: Space
wait: 0.2
expectvalue: Slingshot.Slingshot.ShotsLeft = 1
wait: 3
stop
say: That's a slingshot and breakable blocks, with no code. Materials come from a table, targets are breakable things or things with health, a counter keeps the score, and it all replays to the bit in a rewind and plays in a network game.
